  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A triangle has sides of length $8\\text{ cm}$, $11\\text{ cm}$ and $15\\text{ cm}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the size of the smallest angle in the triangle, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$31.29^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The smallest angle, $\\theta$, is opposite the shortest side, $8\\text{ cm}$. Applying the cosine rule:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{11^2+15^2-8^2}{2(11)(15)}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{47}{55}\\\\\\theta&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{47}{55}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx31.29^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Calculate, correct to two decimal places, the area of the triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$42.85\\text{ cm}^2$\n\nUse the unrounded angle from part a in the triangle area rule.",
          "worked": "Using the unrounded angle $\\theta=\\cos^{-1}(\\frac{47}{55})$ between the $11\\text{ cm}$ and $15\\text{ cm}$ sides:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area}&=\\frac12(11)(15)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\text{Area}&=\\frac{165}{2}\\sin\\left(\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{47}{55}\\right)\\right)\\\\\\text{Area}&\\approx42.85\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Calculate the perimeter of the triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$34\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=8+11+15\\\\P&=34\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p31-q13-heron",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Let ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "s=\\text{half the perimeter of the triangle}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". The area of the triangle can be found using Heron’s formula: ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\text{Area}=\\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", where ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "a,b",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "c",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " are the lengths of the three sides.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p31-q13-d-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Use this formula to calculate the area of the triangle, correct to two decimal places.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$42.85\\text{ cm}^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}s&=\\frac{34}{2}\\\\s&=17\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing Heron’s formula:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area}&=\\sqrt{17(17-8)(17-11)(17-15)}\\\\\\text{Area}&=\\sqrt{1836}\\\\\\text{Area}&=6\\sqrt{51}\\\\\\text{Area}&\\approx42.85\\text{ cm}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
